      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T06:51:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a hazard here if `CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC_RUNTIME_CONFIG` is enabled (so `tcpc_config` is non-const), since `mfd_parent` might change at any time (but presumably only during init). Since we know this can occur if there\u0027s an initialization order problem, this assignment should probably only be done if `CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC_RUNTIME_CONFIG` is disabled (and if it\u0027s enabled always oops).\n\nMore broadly, hitting this code path probably indicates a bug but it\u0027s somewhat useful to avoid crashing if there\u0027s a safe way to do so.",
      "range": {
